## Bundle Optimization

### Code Splitting
```typescript
// Dynamic imports for code splitting
import dynamic from 'next/dynamic';

const HeavyComponent = dynamic(() => import('@/components/HeavyComponent'), {
  loading: () => <Skeleton />,
  ssr: false, // Only if component doesn't need SSR
});

// Route-based code splitting (automatic in Next.js App Router)
// Each route is automatically code-split
```

### Tree Shaking
- Use ES modules (import/export)
- Avoid barrel exports when possible
- Use named exports instead of default exports for utilities
- Remove unused dependencies

### Bundle Analysis
```bash
# Analyze bundle size
npm run build
npx @next/bundle-analyzer
```

### Optimization Strategies
- Remove unused code
- Use smaller alternatives to large libraries
- Lazy load heavy dependencies
- Split vendor chunks appropriately

## Image Optimization

### Next.js Image Component
```typescript
import Image from 'next/image';

<Image
  src="/hero.jpg"
  alt="Hero image"
  width={800}
  height={600}
  priority // For above-the-fold images
  placeholder="blur" // With blurDataURL
  sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, (max-width: 1200px) 50vw, 33vw"
/>
```

### Image Best Practices
- Use Next.js Image component
- Provide width and height
- Use appropriate image formats (WebP, AVIF)
- Implement lazy loading (default)
- Use `priority` for above-the-fold images
- Optimize image sizes before upload
- Use CDN for image delivery

## Caching Strategies

### Next.js Caching
```typescript
// Revalidate every hour
export const revalidate = 3600;

// Fetch with caching
const data = await fetch(url, {
  next: { revalidate: 3600 }, // ISR
});

// Or use cache: 'force-cache' for static data
const data = await fetch(url, {
  cache: 'force-cache',
});
```

### Caching Levels
- **Browser Cache**: Static assets (images, fonts, JS, CSS)
- **CDN Cache**: Edge caching for static content
- **ISR (Incremental Static Regeneration)**: Hybrid static/dynamic
- **Server Cache**: API responses, database queries
- **Client Cache**: React Query, SWR for client state

### Cache Invalidation
```typescript
import { revalidatePath, revalidateTag } from 'next/cache';

// In Server Actions
export async function updateUser() {
  // Update database
  revalidatePath('/users');
  revalidateTag('users');
}
```

## Core Web Vitals

### Largest Contentful Paint (LCP) < 2.5s
- Optimize images (use Next.js Image)
- Preload critical resources
- Reduce server response time
- Eliminate render-blocking resources
- Use CDN for static assets

### First Input Delay (FID) < 100ms
- Reduce JavaScript execution time
- Break up long tasks
- Use code splitting
- Optimize third-party scripts
- Use Web Workers for heavy computations

### Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS) < 0.1
- Set size attributes on images and videos
- Reserve space for ads and embeds
- Avoid inserting content above existing content
- Use font-display: swap for web fonts
- Preload fonts

### Implementation
```typescript
// app/layout.tsx
export default function RootLayout({ children }) {
  return (
    <html>
      <head>
        <link
          rel="preload"
          href="/fonts/inter.woff2"
          as="font"
          type="font/woff2"
          crossOrigin="anonymous"
        />
      </head>
      <body>{children}</body>
    </html>
  );
}
```

## Runtime Performance

### React Optimization
```typescript
// Memoize expensive computations
const expensiveValue = useMemo(() => {
  return computeExpensiveValue(data);
}, [data]);

// Memoize callbacks
const handleClick = useCallback(() => {
  // Handler logic
}, [dependencies]);

// Memoize components
const MemoizedComponent = React.memo(Component, (prevProps, nextProps) => {
  return prevProps.id === nextProps.id;
});
```

### When to Optimize
- Profile first, optimize second
- Use React DevTools Profiler
- Optimize only when there's a performance issue
- Don't over-optimize (premature optimization)

### Virtual Scrolling
```typescript
// For long lists
import { useVirtualizer } from '@tanstack/react-virtual';

const virtualizer = useVirtualizer({
  count: items.length,
  getScrollElement: () => parentRef.current,
  estimateSize: () => 50,
});
```

## Database Query Optimization

### Efficient Queries
```typescript
// Select only needed fields
const users = await prisma.user.findMany({
  select: {
    id: true,
    email: true,
    name: true,
  },
});

// Use pagination
const users = await prisma.user.findMany({
  skip: (page - 1) * pageSize,
  take: pageSize,
});

// Use indexes
// Ensure database indexes are set up for frequently queried fields
```

### Query Patterns
- Avoid N+1 queries (use include)
- Use database indexes
- Implement query result caching
- Use connection pooling
- Batch operations when possible

## API Optimization

### Response Optimization
- Minimize response payload size
- Use compression (gzip, brotli)
- Implement pagination
- Use field selection when possible
- Cache API responses

### Streaming
```typescript
// Stream responses for better perceived performance
export async function GET() {
  const stream = new ReadableStream({
    async start(controller) {
      // Stream data
      controller.enqueue(data);
      controller.close();
    },
  });

  return new Response(stream);
}
```

## Font Optimization

### Font Loading
```typescript
// Preload critical fonts
<link
  rel="preload"
  href="/fonts/inter.woff2"
  as="font"
  type="font/woff2"
  crossOrigin="anonymous"
/>

// Use font-display: swap
@font-face {
  font-family: 'Inter';
  src: url('/fonts/inter.woff2') format('woff2');
  font-display: swap;
}
```

## Third-Party Scripts

### Optimize Third-Party Scripts
- Load asynchronously
- Defer non-critical scripts
- Use next/script component
- Consider self-hosting when possible
- Monitor impact on performance

```typescript
import Script from 'next/script';

<Script
  src="https://example.com/script.js"
  strategy="afterInteractive" // or 'lazyOnload'
  onLoad={() => {
    // Script loaded
  }}
/>
```

